WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
- Hi.

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.659
(audience cheering loudly)

00:00:02.659 --> 00:00:04.481
I'm so excited!

00:00:04.481 --> 00:00:05.314
(The Chicks laughing)

00:00:05.314 --> 00:00:06.570
I'm so excited!

00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:07.960
I was feeling a little under
the weather this morning.

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:10.329
I was like, you get out of bed right now

00:00:10.329 --> 00:00:11.162
(The Chicks chuckling)

00:00:11.162 --> 00:00:12.150
'cause The Chicks are
coming and I'm so excited

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:12.983
y'all are here.

00:00:12.983 --> 00:00:15.290
But two years ago you
changed your band name

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:18.330
and it took me a minute
y'all 'cause I was like

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:20.060
so used to it from childhood.

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:22.230
But then, I heard that this was something

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:25.140
that y'all kinda had in the
making for a while, right?

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:25.973
- Yeah.

00:00:25.973 --> 00:00:26.890
- What was so important to you

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:29.290
to change it to just The Chicks?

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:32.830
- Well, I think just after
George Floyd and all of that,

00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:35.430
we wanted to get rid of
the Dixie part of our name

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:39.890
for a long time, but it seemed
like a huge thing to do.

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:42.250
So we would call, even now
our merch would say DCX

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:44.650
and we always referred to
ourselves as The Chicks.

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:48.040
So it seemed like a really natural change

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:49.700
and it seemed kinda seamless.

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:52.660
- Here's what was cool is
you like educated a lot of us

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:56.070
as well because I had no
idea that it meant anything.

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:57.170
So I had to like goo-,

00:00:57.170 --> 00:00:58.480
I was like, wait, what?

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:01.330
And I was like googling and it
was interesting to find out,

00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:03.116
kind of the origin of
that word and like that.

00:01:03.116 --> 00:01:03.949
- Yeah, I think we did the same.

00:01:03.949 --> 00:01:04.900
I always thought it was a region.

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:06.740
Like if it's, what direction

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:08.110
- South of Mason-Dixon.

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:09.480
- Yeah. Me too.

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:11.270
So it was interesting though.

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:13.470
I thought that was a really cool

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:15.340
to educate the public though on something,

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:17.040
especially at such an important time.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:17.873
- [Natalie] Yeah.

00:01:17.873 --> 00:01:18.990
- So I thought it was really
cool that y'all had done that.

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:21.157
And also it's just like easier to say.

00:01:21.157 --> 00:01:21.990
(The Chicks laughing)

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:22.990
so that's awesome.

00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:25.130
I'm lazy but I love

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:27.550
and then I think everybody
would always say that too.

00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:28.383
Oh, did you see The Chicks?

00:01:28.383 --> 00:01:29.216
Did you see the concert?
- Right.

00:01:29.216 --> 00:01:30.210
- Everybody would always call y'all that.

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:31.141
- Yeah.

00:01:31.141 --> 00:01:32.780
- I think super fans like me.

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:34.240
So what do you each remember

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:37.340
from like the very first time
that y'all played together?

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:38.620
Was it like awkward

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:41.370
or like you knew right
away it was gonna work?

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:44.750
- Well, Natalie had joined
the band, a previous lineup

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:47.590
and so Martie and I were very like nervous.

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:49.410
Like, well she rehearsed all the songs

00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:50.243
and know all the songs.

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:51.915
Natalie was just like,
"oh I got this y'all."

00:01:51.915 --> 00:01:53.103
(Natalie laughs)

00:01:53.103 --> 00:01:53.936
She had this confidence

00:01:53.936 --> 00:01:56.050
and Martie and I are just like, oh my gosh!

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:58.530
But Natalie brought this humongous pad

00:01:58.530 --> 00:01:59.567
with her lyrics on it

00:01:59.567 --> 00:02:02.220
and we just flip it in between songs.

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:04.610
- We played in these two
clubs, outside of Houston.

00:02:04.610 --> 00:02:05.443
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:05.443 --> 00:02:06.406
- And I would just

00:02:06.406 --> 00:02:07.843
(The Chicks laughing)

00:02:07.843 --> 00:02:10.120
bend down, turn the page.

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:12.160
- Oh my God. Do you have a
problem with lyrics? I do.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:15.530
- No, but I had to learn
22 songs in seven days.

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:18.242
I would just listen with headphones

00:02:18.242 --> 00:02:20.598
- And learn to yodel.
- And walk around.

00:02:20.598 --> 00:02:21.981
Yeah, I had never yodeled before.

00:02:21.981 --> 00:02:22.814
(The Chicks laughing)

00:02:22.814 --> 00:02:23.650
- That's a lot.

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:24.610
- [Natalie] I know.

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:26.000
- Oh my gosh!

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:28.810
So the band was famously,
had to be reminded of this.

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:31.050
The band was famously
boycotted on country radio,

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:35.340
19 years ago which feels
like forever ago to me.

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:36.960
But it happened after Natalie,

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:39.360
you spoke out against the war in Iraq

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:40.760
and the president in 2003, right?

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:43.870
So what did you, I ended up,
it was "Shut Up and Sing", right?

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:46.670
The documentary that
came out. I loved that.

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:48.440
I think a lot of artists or anybody

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:52.310
that's under a microscope,
I'm jumping straight to that.

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:53.960
I'm gonna ask the question, but
I'm jumping straight to that

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:57.010
because when you're under a
microscope, everything you say

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.460
even if you don't mean something some way,

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:00.010
or even if it's in a moment,

00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:01.750
everything gets blown out, good or bad.

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:03.650
And it's a very hard way to live

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:05.230
and especially being in an industry,

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:06.820
like I've been told to shut up and sing

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:07.850
and not have an opinion.

00:03:07.850 --> 00:03:10.920
And it's very hard 'cause you're a human

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:14.030
and we all count, our
thoughts and our hearts count.

00:03:14.030 --> 00:03:17.020
So how did y'all deal with that?

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:19.630
That had to be hard after
watching that "Shut Up and Sing".

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:20.463
That was hard.

00:03:20.463 --> 00:03:23.610
Not only on y'all but the
people around you, right?

00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:24.570
- Yeah, I don't know.

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:26.320
I'm a fighter, so I

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:27.153
- [Kelly] I gather

00:03:27.153 --> 00:03:28.219
- like crumble.

00:03:28.219 --> 00:03:31.061
(crowd applauding)

00:03:31.061 --> 00:03:32.110
- That's a Texas woman.

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:34.060
- I did crumble.

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:35.560
After we won all the Grammy's,

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:36.930
I kinda fell apart after that.

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:38.690
I think I was just like in this fight mode

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:41.481
and then it all sort
of came crashing down.

00:03:41.481 --> 00:03:42.510
- Yeah. It's a lotta weight to carry.

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:45.270
- Yeah and it was for how it
was affecting other people.

00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:46.573
I didn't care how it was affecting me.

00:03:46.573 --> 00:03:47.406
- [Kelly] That's what I'm saying.

00:03:47.406 --> 00:03:48.489
- But, yeah.

00:03:48.489 --> 00:03:49.322
(audience applauding)

00:03:49.322 --> 00:03:50.155
- I'm so stunned, I just
can't believe I'm here.

00:03:50.155 --> 00:03:51.550
I remember it's funny, I
was having this moment.

00:03:51.550 --> 00:03:52.383
We were talking about

00:03:52.383 --> 00:03:53.908
'cause the first time we
met, it was on Leno, I think.

00:03:53.908 --> 00:03:54.741
- Yeah.

00:03:54.741 --> 00:03:55.730
- And we were both being interviewed

00:03:55.730 --> 00:03:56.980
and I was like I'm on
the same couch with him.

00:03:56.980 --> 00:03:58.770
And then now you're like on
my couch, I'm interviewing,

00:03:58.770 --> 00:03:59.603
I'm just having a moment.

00:03:59.603 --> 00:04:00.436
(The Chicks laughing)

00:04:00.436 --> 00:04:02.380
Okay. So you're finally
getting back out on the road.

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:03.410
A lot of artists are being able

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:04.243
to get back out on the road

00:04:04.243 --> 00:04:05.980
because of the pandemic,
obviously people couldn't.

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:08.430
So what are some cities
that you're excited to play

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:11.110
like where are you like super stoked?

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:12.379
- Well.

00:04:12.379 --> 00:04:13.690
(Natalie and Martie laughing)

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:15.030
Hartford, Connecticut.

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:15.979
- [Kelly] Are you?

00:04:15.979 --> 00:04:18.292
- Would be one, yes.
- [Kelly] I love it.

00:04:18.292 --> 00:04:19.880
- We have a lot of
family in the Northeast.

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:20.713
- [Kelly] Oh, I didn't know that.

00:04:20.713 --> 00:04:22.640
- we have a lot of Connecticut--

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:23.473
- [Kelly] Ties.

00:04:23.473 --> 00:04:24.720
- Connections. Yes.

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:27.200
- I love Connecticut
connections as soon are there.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.033
- [Emily] Cut that out.

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:29.450
- Clever girl, I know.

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:30.370
I always get excited.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:31.520
There are certain shows I love playing.

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:32.980
Yeah. If my family is there

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:35.020
or just some audiences are amazing.

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:37.000
Like New York's always
an amazing audience.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:39.396
- The state of Ohio is amazing.

00:04:39.396 --> 00:04:40.229
- Yeah.

00:04:40.229 --> 00:04:41.062
(The Chicks laughing)

00:04:41.062 --> 00:04:42.240
Do you know what I find? This is true.

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:44.760
Any state that is hardcore sports ball.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:47.670
Like if they're sports fans,
like if you're like Man Boston,

00:04:47.670 --> 00:04:49.050
that's a fun show to play.

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:49.970
Like they love sports.

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:51.930
They just, they're very passionate people.

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:52.763
- [Natalie] Yeah.

00:04:52.763 --> 00:04:53.676
- So that's true. Ohio is like that.

00:04:53.676 --> 00:04:54.509
- Ohio.

00:04:54.509 --> 00:04:55.342
- My executive producer's from there.

00:04:55.342 --> 00:04:56.175
She's gonna love that.

00:04:56.175 --> 00:04:58.900
So the tour is for your album, Gaslighter.

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:01.270
A lot of people relate to this album

00:05:01.270 --> 00:05:05.940
and the message, I guess from
an artist's point of view,

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:08.700
like how hard is it asking for a friend

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:10.310
while I'm currently writing

00:05:12.515 --> 00:05:13.811
through a similar situation

00:05:13.811 --> 00:05:17.910
is how hard is that to write
so openly and so honest

00:05:17.910 --> 00:05:22.610
while navigating children,
while navigating people?

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:24.850
You're under a microscope
like there's so much?

00:05:24.850 --> 00:05:26.720
I feel like I've written
so many songs myself

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:28.670
for my personal life.

00:05:28.670 --> 00:05:30.680
and I keep kinda keep
going, oh! should I do that?

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:33.660
Or oh God! Did you go through that

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:35.320
like while writing this?

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:38.200
- I definitely wanted to be very blatant

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:40.030
and like literal with this one.

00:05:40.030 --> 00:05:44.310
But yeah, I wasn't like
beyond all the emotion

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:45.280
like I am now.

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:46.390
And then there's a stress of,

00:05:46.390 --> 00:05:48.520
oh my gosh! Now my kids
are gonna hear this.

00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:49.353
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:49.353 --> 00:05:50.600
- Now my son is on tour with us.

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:53.506
He's in the band and I'm
like, this is kinda weird.

00:05:53.506 --> 00:05:54.419
(audience applauding)

00:05:54.419 --> 00:05:56.340
(The Chicks laughing)

00:05:56.340 --> 00:05:57.975
I'm always checking. Are you okay?

00:05:57.975 --> 00:05:59.460
Are you all right?

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:01.350
- Oh my God. I know, 'cause
that could be awkward.

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:02.410
- [Natalie] Yeah.

00:06:02.410 --> 00:06:04.600
- But I love the fact
that like he's an artist.

00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:07.170
So he does get the fact that
like it's very therapeutic

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:09.690
for us to like, that's our outlet.

00:06:09.690 --> 00:06:10.523
- There's no way around it.

00:06:10.523 --> 00:06:12.810
When you write falsely, it doesn't work.

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:14.557
- It's transparent that
you're full of crap, yeah.

00:06:14.557 --> 00:06:15.640
- [Emily] You have to be real.

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:17.163
- Agreed. Sorry I'm so blunt.

00:06:17.163 --> 00:06:17.996
(audience laughing)

00:06:17.996 --> 00:06:19.990
- It's weird. The more specific you are,

00:06:19.990 --> 00:06:22.716
the more it's universal to other people.

00:06:22.716 --> 00:06:23.643
(audience applauding)

00:06:23.643 --> 00:06:25.642
- Which, isn't that so sad?

00:06:25.642 --> 00:06:26.720
- Yeah, I know.

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:28.340
- I mean life is so hard.

00:06:28.340 --> 00:06:29.980
Yeah. It's sad that people relate.

00:06:29.980 --> 00:06:32.243
Okay. So we all went through divorces.

00:06:33.446 --> 00:06:37.130
And how did you each find
strength and not just music?

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:39.410
I think it's therapeutic, but
like your female friendships.

00:06:39.410 --> 00:06:41.700
I feel like that has really helped me.

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:44.090
- Yeah. I remember when
you first came down

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:46.537
in the studio in Nashville and said,

00:06:46.537 --> 00:06:48.770
"Guys, I just wanna tell
you I'm getting a divorce."

00:06:48.770 --> 00:06:49.992
- Which time was this?

00:06:49.992 --> 00:06:50.825
(The Chicks laughing)

00:06:50.825 --> 00:06:53.020
(Kelly laughs)

00:06:53.020 --> 00:06:53.853
- Oh my gosh!

00:06:53.853 --> 00:06:55.130
- It's the first one. Number One.

00:06:56.770 --> 00:06:59.820
I remember thinking, well,
I'm getting a divorce.

00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:01.480
Now, she says, she's getting a divorce.

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:03.060
Now, I can't say I'm getting a divorce.

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:04.427
It was kind but then I(indistinct)

00:07:04.427 --> 00:07:05.260
- but me saying it.
- You haven't told her.

00:07:05.260 --> 00:07:07.140
- I hadn't told y'all.

00:07:07.140 --> 00:07:09.640
I was feeling like
everybody was gonna judge me

00:07:09.640 --> 00:07:11.980
'cause I was like I thought I
was first getting the divorce.

00:07:11.980 --> 00:07:13.500
- [Kelly] You Kept that in!

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:14.532
- Yeah.

00:07:14.532 --> 00:07:15.366
(Kelly laughs)

00:07:15.366 --> 00:07:16.650
- So I was like, guys,
I'm getting a divorce.

00:07:16.650 --> 00:07:19.614
And Martie's like, I'm
having a horrible marriage.

00:07:19.614 --> 00:07:20.830
(The Chicks laughing)

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:22.300
- Oh my Gosh.

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:24.180
- We'll do this together because I felt,

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:26.410
'cause I didn't know anybody close to me

00:07:26.410 --> 00:07:30.020
that was getting a divorce,
so I was so happy for you.

00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:31.782
- Yeah, we were divorced buddies.

00:07:31.782 --> 00:07:33.380
- But it is something to talk about

00:07:33.380 --> 00:07:35.550
'cause there is a level of like shame,

00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:39.660
and like guilt and people
especially from where we're from.

00:07:39.660 --> 00:07:41.960
It's like you stick it out and it's like,

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:44.550
oh, that's what I've been doing, you know?

00:07:44.550 --> 00:07:45.419
And I dunno if I can do it.

00:07:45.419 --> 00:07:46.252
- [Natalie] Yeah.

00:07:46.252 --> 00:07:48.510
I dunno if I can continue
that for both of you.

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:52.210
Like obviously it's not working
and people aren't happy.

00:07:52.210 --> 00:07:53.043
So it's a hard thing.

00:07:53.043 --> 00:07:55.490
I can't imagine holding that in.

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:57.620
Like I had to finally,

00:07:57.620 --> 00:07:58.980
I can't imagine holding it in for a while

00:07:58.980 --> 00:07:59.990
and then you finally say it.

00:07:59.990 --> 00:08:03.830
But the release of that is so monumental.

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:05.970
I don't know, I felt like
it was for me. Did you?

00:08:05.970 --> 00:08:08.430
- Oh yeah. But I didn't
have kids with that one

00:08:08.430 --> 00:08:09.320
and she didn't either.

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:12.670
And I think it's so much harder
when you've got your babies.

00:08:12.670 --> 00:08:16.590
- Yeah, it is. That's where
the decision making sucks.

00:08:16.590 --> 00:08:19.070
So what does it mean to
have your kids performing

00:08:19.070 --> 00:08:21.250
with you on this tour
'cause that's pretty cool?

00:08:21.250 --> 00:08:22.083
- It's awesome.

00:08:22.083 --> 00:08:24.673
Slade's 21. He can play everything.

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:26.667
- [Kelly] Could drink legally.

00:08:26.667 --> 00:08:28.145
- Bit right, isn't it?

00:08:28.145 --> 00:08:29.343
(The Chicks laughing)

00:08:29.343 --> 00:08:31.240
I don't worry about that.

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:33.030
And Martie's daughter's gonna play

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:33.863
- [Martie] She's 18

00:08:33.863 --> 00:08:34.970
- [Natalie] Violin.

00:08:34.970 --> 00:08:36.312
She plays piano and violin.

00:08:36.312 --> 00:08:37.145
- Wow.

00:08:37.145 --> 00:08:40.690
- But she's gonna play violin,
maybe try some accordion.

00:08:40.690 --> 00:08:43.930
But I wanna say Slade is
just as good as anybody

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:46.238
in the band. It's not a charity case.

00:08:46.238 --> 00:08:47.440
